Local Zero Hour Reforged SDL 3.4.16 Vulkan ray query extension.
This is a downstream private bridge, not an upstream SDL contribution.
Opt-in property zhr.vulkan.ray_query enables Vulkan 1.2 plus supported ray-query
features. Ordinary SDL device creation is unchanged. Implementation sidecars
are maintained beside this patch and copied by Tools/vendor.sh. The private
command guard checks device identity in every mode and follows SDL debug-only
submitted/pass bookkeeping validation when command buffers are recycled.
Sidecars also provide a water closest-hit compute layout (80-byte push constants,
RGBA32F hit output and TLAS), retaining the original sun-shadow ABI.
Full water-path sidecars add a separate 112-byte layout for primary, sun and
continuation transport, with sampled packed geometry and two RGBA32F outputs.

Optional property zhr.vulkan.ray_query_optional probes loader API support without
changing SDL adapter ranking; device augmentation failure retries the same adapter
with original features/extensions. Missing native functions clear the capability.

Optional hardware capability excludes CPU/OTHER only after normal adapter selection.

